The native `ValSeq` predicate approach still left an impossible non-integer branch syntactically alive, so I replaced it with a proof-only symbolic integer-sequence generator whose two iterator equations are literal specializations of the supplied list rules. The loop proof is now running through clean integer induction cases; I’m checking whether the end-to-end claim can consume that lemma automatically or needs the standard trusted-lemma staging.
